//~ ErrorDupName:1 "conflicting definition"
// A submodule whose designated file has no 'mod' line: the folder bare/ names
// it, and every module's first file opens with the line restating that name,
// so its first statement is refused. It is still the module bare/ names, and a
// declaration of the parent spelling 'bare' collides with it. With no
// declaration to be reported at, this module's half of that diagnostic is
// reported at the first line of this file -- the file that makes bare/ a
// module, which is the nearest thing the module has to one. The annotation on
// line 1 is that half.

pub fn bareFn(n i64) i64 {   //~ ErrorNoModDcl:1 "begin it with 'mod bare;'"
  n;
}
